# Test hints for CSVProcessor
# Requires managed plugin: https://github.com/arolang/plugin-rust-csv
#
# Interpreter only. The expected output used to be the banner line alone, with
# a note that the plugin might not load; that assertion held whether or not the
# plugin worked. Pinning the real output (GitLab #820) showed it does not work
# in compiled mode: `aro build --static` compiles the Rust staticlib and
# renames its symbols, and the compiled binary still answers
#   Cannot parsecsv the parsed from the csv-data.
# so the plugin's actions are not resolvable at run time. SQLiteExample fails
# the same way; HashPluginDemo's C plugin and QualifierPlugin's Swift
# qualifiers work compiled. That is a bug to fix in the build/runtime
# (GitLab #884), not an expectation to weaken, so this example asserts the
# interpreter's full output until it is; restoring `mode: both` is that
# issue's acceptance test.
mode: interpreter
occurrence-check: true
